# Restart charts on the measurable separated simple-prefix configuration

Packet PROVE-AUX61-R1, continuation of the original-target construction.

`has_original_target_restart_chart_on_configuration` constructs the inherited
chart on the full measurable geometric event. Simplicity and interiority of
the own prefix, positive tip clearance, target protection and access incidence
are properties of this event, not global assumptions on every ambient sample.

`has_countable_charted_clearance_cover` gives an exact measurable countable
cover at the fixed rational original own time, with uniform positive rational
lower bounds on tip height and counterflow clearance. Every piece carries
the full original-target chart, with the literal inherited derivative phase
and both prime-end limits.

The compact-open path-space tests and the hitting-measurable random-tip
distance use only retained observations. No future own value is inspected
to select the component or its chart. This does not establish a conditional
field kernel, a disintegration, or coverage of the consumer's crossing event
by such geometric configurations. R48 and R77 remain in force.
